LICENSING STATUS — MIXED PROVENANCE RESEARCH REPOSITORY

This file records scope; it does not grant a new blanket license or relicense
third-party material.

Existing per-file copyright notices and license terms remain in force. The
truck_bringup and nav_virtual_lanes package manifests declare Apache-2.0. A copy
of the Apache License 2.0 is provided in LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt for components to
which that license applies.

Historical truck_bringup/setup.py declared MIT while package.xml declared
Apache-2.0. Those conflicting records do not establish permission to assign one
license to every file. The inactive metadata is preserved under historical/.

The experimental nav_virtual_lanes_planner previously had no resolved license.
LicenseRef-Provenance-Review-Required is a status marker, not a license grant.
Imagery, heightmaps, meshes, CAD-derived content, marks and adapted external
utilities require the provenance review described in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and
PUBLICATION_ASSET_AUDIT.md. A code-package license does not establish rights to
those assets. Rights for unresolved material must be confirmed by its rights
holder before redistribution outside any applicable existing permission.

No license is inferred from public GitHub availability or from a model export
tool's metadata. Dataset licensing is governed separately by the Zenodo record.
